  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1>How we write our guides.</h1>

      <h2>Who writes them</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/about">Bryce Wachtell</a>, founder of ScamPrep, writes our guides and is
        responsible for every word in them. Bryce works full time on scam prevention for older
        adults and their families. He isn't a lawyer or a financial advisor, so our guides are
        education, not legal or financial advice. The expertise comes from the primary sources
        we cite, plus our own experience building ScamPrep.
      </p>

      <h2>Where the facts come from</h2>
      <p>
        We rely on primary sources: the agencies that track scams and run the programs
        scammers impersonate, such as the Federal Trade Commission, the FBI's Internet Crime
        Complaint Center, the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau and Medicare. Each guide lists
        its sources at the end.
      </p>

      <h2>The advice we give</h2>
      <p>
        We teach one habit above all: end the contact, then check through a phone number or
        website you already trust. We never suggest keeping a scammer talking, testing them,
        or playing along. We only recommend steps that a trusted source recommends.
      </p>
      <p>
        Examples of scam messages and calls are labeled "Simulated." When we share a real
        story, it's with the person's permission, and we change details that could identify them.
      </p>

      <h2>Standards and ethics</h2>
      <p>
        ScamPrep is a company, and our guides mention what we're building. They never rank us
        against other products, and we don't accept payment to mention or link to anyone.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        If you spot a mistake, email <a href="mailto:hello@getscamprep.com">hello@getscamprep.com</a>
        and we'll fix it. If a correction changes the advice in a guide, we say so at the end
        of that guide, with the date.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/guides">Read our guides</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
